_3D.RobotArmAnimations.setTable [SimTalk]
Sets the table that contains the Robot Arm Animations of the object designated by <Path>.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>._3D.RobotArmAnimations.setTable(Animations:table
Parameter
The parameter Animations of data type table designates the table which contains the robot animations.
The table has three columns:
• The column From of data type string indicates at which object a robot arm animation starts.
It designates the default orientation as the starting point if the cell is empty.
• The column To of data type string indicates to which object a robot arm animation moves.
It designates the default orientation as the destination if the cell is empty.
• The column Table of data type table indicates the robot arm animation <Path>.
It is a subtable with three columns of data type length for the X, Y, and Z values of all coordinates which
the robot is to pass on its route from the From position to the To position within the coordinate system
of the robot.
Example
var t : table
PickAndPlace1._3D.RobotArmAnimations.getTable(t)
PickAndPlace2._3D.RobotArmAnimations.setTable(t)
See also
_3D.RobotArmAnimations.getTable [SimTalk]
