JointVelocity [SimTalk]
Sets the speed of the joint of the object designated by <Path>.
Remarks
An animatable object with the Velocity of 0 does not rotate with the Turntable when the Turntable
rotates. This applies when the insertion position of the animatable object is located on the animation
rotation axis of the Turntable. This is the case if the insertion point is exactly located on the animation
rotation center or is reachable from there along the animation rotation axis without a sideways deviation.
This behavior resembles a real Turntable with a fixed base and a rotating table.
_3D.getObject enables you to access animatable objects.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.JointVelocity:speed
Assignment Value
The specified value designates:
• The velocity in meters per second for a Prismatic Joint.
For a Prismatic Joint you assign a value of data type speed.
• The angular velocity in degrees per second for a Revolute Joint.
For a Revolute Joint you assign a value of data type real.
JointVelocity [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 12-909
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

