moveTo [SimTalk]
Moves to one or several positions or rotations of the joint of the object designated by <Path>.
Remarks
A moveTo call of an animatable object aborts a previous moveTo run of the same animatable object. For
active movements to poses or movements, which the method _3D.Poses.moveToCoordinate started, a
conflict arises if this animatable object is part of the other active movement.
Note
Whenever you change Limits, Velocity, Acceleration, or the Joint Type of the animatable object, the
initial position for the next pose run that affects this object returns to 0.
Note
Plant Simulation does not use joint limits in this method. This means, that you can move to a position
beyond the limits you specified.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.moveTo(PositionOrRotationAngle:real[, TimeSpan:time]) → time
<Path>.moveTo(PositionsOrRotationAngles:array[real][, TimeSpan:time]) → 
time
<Path>.moveTo(PositionsOrRotationAngles:array[real][, 
TimeSpans:array[time]]) → time
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter PositionOrRotationAngle of data type real sets the position or the rotation angle of the
joint toward which the object moves.
The parameter PositionsOrRotationAngles designates an array of data type real that sets a sequence of
positions or rotation angles of the joint to which the object moves. The designated positions or rotations
are then approached sequentially one after the other.
The movement stays active until the last position or rotation is reached.
• The optional parameter TimeSpan of data type time sets the duration of the movement.
moveTo [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 12-911
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

The optional parameter TimeSpans designates an array of data type time, which sets the durations of
the movement.
Do not specify the parameter to run the pose movement with the time which results from the speeds
from the joint definitions of the involved animatable object.
If you specify the parameter, it means the following:
◦ If you specify a single time, the entire movement has to take place within the specified time.
◦ If you specify a sequence of times in an array, the first position or rotation is to be reached within
the first time span, the second pose in the second time span, etc. You have to specify as many time
spans as you defined positions or rotations.
You can only specify an array of times if you also specified an array of positions or rotations.
The instruction Station._3D.getObject(1).moveTo(3, [7.5]) results in an error although
the same number of positions is specified as the number of time spans. The instruction
Station._3D.getObject(1).moveTo([3], [7.5]) does not result in an error, but is
unnecessarily complicated because the instruction Station._3D.getObject(1).moveTo(3,
7.5)) yields the same result without specifying an array at all.
Return Value
The return value has the data type time.
It designates the time span of the simulation time which the designated pose movement will probably
take, provided it will not be interrupted.
Example
Station._3D.getObject(1).moveTo(3, -1)
Station._3D.getObject(1).moveTo([3, -1], 7.5)
Station._3D.getObject(1).moveTo(3, 7.5)
