moveToMUAnimationPosition [SimTalk]
Moves the joint designated by <Path> to the position and rotation in space where the specified MU
instance would be located when being moved to the specified place.
Remarks
When moving a joint to a MU instance, Plant Simulation computes the target joint state based upon a
relaxed state at which the origin of the joint is located at the position [0,0,0]. The joint points toward the
direction specified in the attribute _3D.AniTranslationDirection in its reset coordinate system.
If the destination is length-oriented,moveToMUAnimationPosition of animatable objects computes a
movement, which deposits the front of the MU at the destination instead of the booking point. For
place-oriented objects nothing changes.
Note
Plant Simulation does not use joint limits in this method. This means, that you can move to a position
beyond the limits you specified.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.moveToMUAnimationPosition(MU:object, TargetPE:object/PE[, RelPos/
AbsPos:real/length, TimeSpan:time]) -> time
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter MU of data type object designates the MU instance to measure when moving to the
target place.
• The parameter TargetPE of data type object designates the place to which the item is to move. This can
be a specific PE (production element) or an object if the object only has one PE.
• The optional parameter RelPos/AbsPos designates a value of data type real or length.
If the value has the data type real, it designates the relative position on the object. The relative position
can be a value between 0 and 1. 0 designates the start of the animation and 1 the end of the animation,
i.e., the value 100 %.
If the value has the data type length, it designates the absolute position on the object as the distance
starting at the beginning of the object.
moveToMUAnimationPosition [SimTalk]
12-918 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

This parameter will only be used if TargetPE specifies a length-oriented place, e.g. a Conveyor or a
Transporter with a length-oriented loadbay.
If you do not specify the parameter, it takes the value 0.0.
• The optional parameter TimeSpan of data type time designates the duration of the movement.
If you do not specify the parameter, Plant Simulation runs the movement run with the time which
results from the speed from the joint definition of this animatable object.
Return Value
The return value has the data type time.
It designates the time span of the simulation time which the designated movement will probably take,
provided it will not be interrupted.
Example
var mu = otherObject.cont
var arm = self.~._3D.getObject("Arm")
wait arm.moveToMUAnimationPosition(mu)
