_3D.MovementInterruptible [SimTalk]
Sets if failures and pauses will interrupt pose runs of the object designated by <Path> (true) or not
(false).
Remarks
If you start a pose run while a failure or pause is active at the moment, the pose run will start regardless
of the setting MovementInterruptible.
A pose run designates all movements that were started by any version of the methods _3D.Poses.moveTo
and _3D.Poses.moveToCoordinate, both for the object itself and for any of its animatable objects.
_3D.MovementInterruptible applies to the objects FluidSource, FluidDrain, Tank, Mixer, Transporter,
Frame, Exporter, and Worker. It also applies to all objects which can transport MUs or Workers, except
for the Workplace.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>._3D.MovementInterruptible:boolean
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type boolean.
Example
Station._3D.MovementInterruptible := true
See also
Movement Interruptible
