_3D.Poses.cancelMovement [SimTalk]
Cancels the movement toward the designated pose of the object designated by <Path>.
Remarks
If you do not specify the optional parameter, all movements will be canceled.
_3D.Poses.cancelMovement affects the designated pose, however always together with the other poses to
which the object moved together with this pose in a common call of the method _3D.Poses.moveTo.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>._3D.Poses.cancelMovement([Pose:string])
Parameter
The optional parameter Pose of data type string sets the name of the pose toward which the object moves.
Example
Station._3D.Poses.moveTo(["Pose1", "Pose2"])
Station._3D.Poses.cancelMovement("Pose1") 
// instead, you can also enter:
Station._3D.Poses.cancelMovement("Pose2")
See also
_3D.Poses.moveTo [SimTalk]
_3D.Poses.pauseMovement [SimTalk]
_3D.Poses.stopMovement [SimTalk]
_3D.MovementInterruptible [SimTalk]
