_3D.Poses.continueMovement [SimTalk]
Continues the movement the designated pose of the object designated by <Path>.
Remarks
If you do not specify the optional parameter, all paused movements will be continued.
_3D.Poses.continueMovement affects the designated pose, however always together with the other poses
to which the object moved together with this pose in a common call of the method _3D.Poses.moveTo.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>._3D.Poses.continueMovement([Pose:string])
Parameter
The optional parameter Pose of data type string sets the name of the pose which the object moves.
If you do not specify the optional parameter, all paused movements will be continued.
Example
Station._3D.Poses.moveTo(["Pose1", "Pose2"])
Station._3D.Poses.continueMovement("Pose1") 
// instead, you can also enter:
Station._3D.Poses.continueMovement("Pose2")
