_3D.Poses.getAnimationTime [SimTalk]
Returns how long the movement toward the designated pose of the object designated by <Path> takes.
Remarks
If you do not specify the optional parameter, the method returns the simulation time which remains until
all pose movements and movements caused by the methods _3D.Poses.moveToCoordinate or moveTo
respectively, are processed, provided that _3D.Poses.pauseMovement does not cause a delay.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>._3D.Poses.getAnimationTime([Pose:string])
Parameter
The optional parameter Pose of data type string sets the name of the pose toward which the object moves.
Example
print Station._3D.Poses.getAnimationTime
print Station._3D.Poses.getAnimationTime("Pose1")
SimTalk
_3D.Poses.moveToCoordinate [SimTalk]
_3D.Poses.pauseMovement [SimTalk]
moveTo [SimTalk]
_3D.Poses.getAnimationTime [SimTalk]
